<p class="lead">Published in 1972, Knockers examines the Australian habit of denigrating success and cutting down 'tall poppies', part of Dunstan's quartet of books on national character alongside Wowsers, Sports and Ratbags.</p>
<hr>
<div class="row">
  <div class="col-12 col-md-3">
    <img src="{{ '/img/knockers.jpg' | url }}" class="img-fluid" alt="Cover of the book">
  </div>
  <div class="col-12 col-md-9">
    <h3 class="h5">From the original dust jacket</h3>
    <p>Drawing on historical anecdote and press cuttings, Keith Dunstan traces the knocker from colonial times to the present, the Australian who takes a special delight in cutting down anyone who succeeds.</p>
  </div>
</div>
